s":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"பாடு","gloss":"praise"},{"text":"பெறு","lemma":"பெறு","gloss":"receive"}],"gloss":"praise-receiving"},{"surface":"பரிசிலன்","parts":[{"text":"பரிசில்","lemma":"பரிசில்","gloss":"gift"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"he who has"}],"gloss":"recipient of gifts"},{"surface":"வாடினன்","parts":[{"text":"வாடு","lemma":"வாடு","gloss":"fade/wither"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"having faded"},{"surface":"பெயர்தல்","parts":[{"text":"பெயர்","lemma":"பெயர்","gloss":"move/return"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"தல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"returning"},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நாடு","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"நாடு","gloss":"country"}],"gloss":"country"},{"surface":"இழந்ததனினும்","parts":[{"text":"இழந்ததனினும்","lemma":"இழந்ததனினும்","gloss":"even more than losing"}],"gloss":"even more than losing","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நனி","parts":[{"text":"நனி","lemma":"நனி","gloss":"much"}],"gloss":"much"},{"surface":"இன்னாது","parts":[{"text":"இன்னாது","lemma":"இன்னாது","gloss":"painful"}],"gloss":"painful","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"say"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"thus"}],"gloss":"saying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வாள்","parts":[{"text":"வாள்","lemma":"வாள்","gloss":"sword"}],"gloss":"sword"},{"surface":"தந்தனனே","parts":[{"text":"தந்தனனே","lemma":"தந்தனனே","gloss":"he gave indeed"}],"gloss":"he gave indeed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தலை","parts":[{"text":"தலை","lemma":"தலை","gloss":"head"}],"gloss":"head"},{"surface":"எனக்கு","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"I"},{"text":"அக்கு","lemma":"அக்கு","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to me"},{"surface":"ஈய","parts":[{"text":"ஈ","lemma":"ஈ","gloss":"give"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to give"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தன்னின்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"தான்","gloss":"himself"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"than"}],"gloss":"than himself"},{"surface":"சிறந்தது","parts":[{"text":"சிறந்தது","lemma":"சிறந்தது","gloss":"that which is greater"}],"gloss":"that which is greater","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பிறிதுஒன்று","parts":[{"text":"பிறிது","lemma":"பிறிது","gloss":"other"},{"text":"ஒன்று","lemma":"ஒன்று","gloss":"one"}],"gloss":"another thing"},{"surface":"இன்மையின்","parts":[{"text":"இன்மை","lemma":"இன்மை","gloss":"absence"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"because of"}],"gloss":"because of absence"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆடுமலி","parts":[{"text":"ஆடு","lemma":"ஆடு","gloss":"victory/dance"},{"text":"மலி","lemma":"மலி","gloss":"abundant"}],"gloss":"victory-filled"},{"surface":"உவகையோடு","parts":[{"text":"உவகை","lemma":"உவகை","gloss":"joy"},{"text":"ஓடு","lemma":"ஓடு","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with joy"},{"surface":"வருவல்","parts":[{"text":"வரு","lemma":"வரு","gloss":"come"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"I come"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஓடா","parts":[{"text":"ஓடு","lemma":"ஓடு","gloss":"run/retreat"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"negative participle"}],"gloss":"unretreating"},{"surface":"பூட்கை","parts":[{"text":"பூட்கை","lemma":"பூட்கை","gloss":"resolve"}],"gloss":"resolve"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"கிழமையோன்","parts":[{"text":"கிழமை","lemma":"கிழமை","gloss":"friendship/lordship"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ஓன்","gloss":"he who has"}],"gloss":"your lord/friend"},{"surface":"கண்டே","parts":[{"text":"கண்டே","lemma":"கண்டே","gloss":"having seen indeed"}],"gloss":"having seen indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"In the impermanent world, those who intended to endure / established their fame and perished themselves. / The wealthy who rose high with difficult-to-approach excellence, / because of not giving to those who beg in poverty, / do not know the relationship of ancient people. / Sounding bells hanging low to the feet echoing on the adorned forehead / of the moving-with-grace elephant, to those who sing, unstintingly / giving, the lord of the strong horse of indestructible good fame, / having sung, while I stood, in vain / 'My returning, as a praise-receiving recipient of gifts, having faded, / is much more painful than losing my country,' saying, / he gave his sword, for me to give his head, / because of the absence of another thing greater than himself. / With victory-filled joy, I come, / having seen indeed your lord of unretreating resolve.","translation":"In this impermanent world, those who desired to leave an enduring mark established their fame and then passed away. But the wealthy, who rose high with unapproachable excellence, yet failed to give to the poor who begged of them, remain forgotten, unknown to the generations of old. I stood singing of the lord of indestructible fame and swift horses, who unstintingly gives elephants with adorned foreheads and low-hanging sounding bells to those who sing his praise. Seeing me, he thought, 'For a renowned bard to leave my presence empty-handed and withered is far more painful than losing my own kingdom.' Having nothing else greater than himself to offer, he handed me his sword to take his head. Now, filled with triumphant joy, I return, having witnessed the unwavering resolve of your noble lord.","modern":"நிலையற்ற இவ்வுலகில் நிலைத்து நிற்க விரும்பியவர்கள், தங்கள் புகழை நிலைநிறுத்திவிட்டுத் தாமே மறைந்து போயினர். அணுக முடியாத சிறப்பினைப் பெற்று உயர்ந்த செல்வர்கள், வறுமையால் இரப்போர்க்கு ஈயாத காரணத்தால், பழங்கால மக்களின் உறவை அறியாதவர் ஆயினர். காலில் விழும் ஒலியெழுப்பும் மணிகள் அசையும் நெற்றியைக் கொண்ட, அசைந்து நடக்கும் யானைகளைப் பாடுவோர்க்குக் குறையாமல் வழங்கும், அழியாத நல்ல புகழையும் வலிமையான குதிரையையும் உடைய தலைவனைப் பாடி நான் நின்றேன். அப்போது அவன், 'புகழ் பெற்ற பரிசிலன் வறுமையால் வாடித் திரும்புவது, என் நாட்டை இழந்ததைக் காட்டிலும் மிகவும் துன்பமானது' என்று கூறி, எனக்குக் கொடுப்பதற்குத் தன்னை விடச் சிறந்த பொருள் வேறு ஒன்றும் இல்லாததால், தன் தலையை வெட்டி எடுத்துக்கொள்ளுமாறு தன் வாளைத் தந்தான். அஞ்சாத மனவலிமை கொண்ட உனது தலைவனைக் கண்டு, பெருமகிழ்ச்சியோடு நான் வருகின்றேன்.","explanation":"This poem is set in the Purattinai of Padan, under the theme of Parisil Vidai (taking leave with gifts). The poet Perunthalai Sathanar is speaking to Ilankumanan, the younger brother of Kumanan. Kumanan, a generous chieftain, had been exiled to the forest by his brother, who also placed a bounty on Kumanan's head. When the poet visited Kumanan in the forest and sang of his plight, Kumanan had nothing left to give. Feeling that letting a bard leave empty-handed was worse than losing his kingdom, Kumanan offered his sword to the poet, urging him to cut off his head and claim the bounty. The poet, deeply moved by this supreme sacrifice, returns to the brother with the sword, praising Kumanan's unmatched resolve and teaching a lesson in true generosity.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.8,1.2],[1.2,1.6],[1.6,2.6],[2.6,2.6],[2.6,2.96],[2.96,3.14],[3.7,4.7],[4.7,4.8],[4.8,5.4],[5.4,5.7],[5.7,6.9],[6.9,7.1],[7.1,7.43],[7.43,8.5],[8.5,9.3],[9.3,9.5],[9.5,9.9],[9.9,10.3],[10.3,10.3],[10.3,12.3],[12.3,12.4],[12.4,13.2],[13.2,14.0],[14.0,14.1],[14.1,14.5],[14.5,15.58],[15.58,16.5],[16.5,16.6],[16.6,17.2],[17.2,17.6],[18.72,19.22],[19.22,19.82],[19.82,20.22],[20.22,20.52],[20.52,21.72],[21.72,22.42],[22.49,22.92],[22.92,23.42],[23.42,23.62],[23.62,24.86],[24.86,25.42],[25.42,25.42],[25.42,25.92],[25.92,26.42],[26.42,27.22],[27.22,27.22],[27.22,27.82],[27.82,28.32],[28.42,28.86],[29.21,29.32],[29.32,29.82],[29.82,30.42],[30.42,30.92],[30.92,31.52],[31.52,31.92],[31.92,32.12],[32.12,33.32],[33.32,33.81],[33.96,34.32],[34.32,34.48]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.9],[0.9,1.3],[1.3,1.7],[1.7,3.0],[3.0,3.0],[3.0,3.42],[3.42,3.63],[4.3,5.4],[5.4,5.5],[5.5,6.1],[6.1,6.5],[6.5,7.9],[7.9,8.1],[8.1,8.5],[8.5,9.8],[9.8,10.6],[10.6,10.8],[10